{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end... and Pharaoh dreamed.</b> While he was dreaming the matters of his thoughts, he also dreamed that he was standing on the bank of the Nile, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Berakhot 55a): כְּשֵׁם שֶׁאִי אֶפְשָׁר לְבָר בְּלֹא תֶּבֶן, כָּךְ אִי אֶפְשָׁר לַחֲלוֹם בְּלֹא דְּבָרִים בְּטֵלִים (just as it is impossible to winnow without straw, so too it is impossible to dream without idle things)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:03.473648390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}